From: Henk Wiedig <hwiedig@googlemail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: wave5: expose cyclic intra refresh

The Wave5 firmware can refresh a picture in bands of intra-coded CTU rows
(gradual decoder refresh), and wave5_set_enc_openparam already turns an
intra_refresh_mode/arg pair into the firmware's rows-per-picture setting.
Nothing sets that pair, so the feature is unreachable from V4L2.

Register the standard V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD (cyclic
only) and map a non-zero period, in pictures, onto REFRESH_MODE_CTU_ROWS.
Combined with GOP_SIZE 0 this gives an encode with no periodic IDR, whose
cost is spread evenly over the pictures instead of one large keyframe.

Applied on top of the MissingLynk ml-kernel wave5 patches.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-enc.c	2026-10-01 10:25:05.790285620 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-enc.c	2026-10-01 10:25:05.807495273 +0200
@@ -1178,6 +1178,19 @@
 	case V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_REFRESH_PERIOD:
 		inst->enc_param.intra_period = ctrl->val;
 		break;
+	case V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD_TYPE:
+		/* Only cyclic is registered: the firmware sweeps CTU rows. */
+		break;
+	case V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD:
+		/*
+		 * Cyclic intra refresh (GDR): the firmware codes a band of CTU rows
+		 * as intra in every picture, so the whole picture is refreshed over
+		 * this many pictures without an IDR. wave5_set_enc_openparam turns
+		 * the period into rows per picture. 0 turns it off.
+		 */
+		inst->enc_param.intra_refresh_mode = ctrl->val ? REFRESH_MODE_CTU_ROWS : 0;
+		inst->enc_param.intra_refresh_arg = ctrl->val;
+		break;
 	case V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_LOSSLESS_CU:
 		inst->enc_param.lossless_enable = ctrl->val;
 		break;
@@ -2005,6 +2018,14 @@
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(v4l2_ctrl_hdl, &wave5_vpu_enc_ctrl_ops,
 			  V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_REFRESH_PERIOD,
 			  0, 2047, 1, 0);
+	v4l2_ctrl_new_std_menu(v4l2_ctrl_hdl, &wave5_vpu_enc_ctrl_ops,
+			       V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD_TYPE,
+			       V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD_TYPE_CYCLIC,
+			       ~(1 << V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD_TYPE_CYCLIC),
+			       V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD_TYPE_CYCLIC);
+	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(v4l2_ctrl_hdl, &wave5_vpu_enc_ctrl_ops,
+			  V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_INTRA_REFRESH_PERIOD,
+			  0, 2047, 1, 0);
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(v4l2_ctrl_hdl, &wave5_vpu_enc_ctrl_ops,
 			  V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_LOSSLESS_CU,
 			  0, 1, 1, 0);
